WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:07.080
So now the question is why do we need temporary tables?

00:07.120 --> 00:08.480
Let's see the following scenario.

00:08.520 --> 00:11.920
Now let's say that in our source database we have a table called orders.

00:11.960 --> 00:15.240
And now we would like to go and load the table in our data warehouse.

00:15.240 --> 00:20.280
We have to do several transformations in order to prepare the data for the analysis in the data warehouse.

00:20.320 --> 00:24.800
So maybe you have one query to remove the duplicates and another one to handle the nulls.

00:24.960 --> 00:27.440
And maybe you are doing filtering and cleaning up.

00:27.560 --> 00:29.800
And the last step you would like to aggregate the data.

00:29.840 --> 00:35.840
And now of course those queries those transformations want to change the content of the table orders.

00:35.880 --> 00:40.160
And there is no scenario where you can do that directly on the source database.

00:40.200 --> 00:41.760
And of course this is not allowed.

00:41.960 --> 00:46.360
That's why in data warehousing we have to go and get our own copy of the data.

00:46.360 --> 00:49.720
And then on top of this data we can do our transformations.

00:49.760 --> 00:52.520
Now one way to do this using the temporary tables.

00:52.520 --> 00:58.120
So you have one script in order to extract the data from the table orders and put it in a temporary

00:58.160 --> 01:00.280
table as an intermediate result.

01:00.280 --> 01:05.680
And then you come with the transformations and all those queries, and they start manipulating and changing

01:05.680 --> 01:09.240
the data of this extra copy in that temporary table.

01:09.280 --> 01:14.880
And the last step you have the load where you can load the final version of the intermediate results

01:14.880 --> 01:15.920
in the database.

01:15.960 --> 01:20.560
This is if you would like to do the whole ETL before inserting the data to the database.

01:20.640 --> 01:24.590
So now the orders table and the final table in the data warehouse.

01:24.590 --> 01:27.350
Both of them are tables, so they are permanent.

01:27.390 --> 01:27.830
Tables.

01:27.830 --> 01:30.750
And they will stay there as long as we don't drop them.

01:30.750 --> 01:31.910
So they are very important.

01:31.950 --> 01:32.510
Tables.

01:32.710 --> 01:34.750
But now for the intermediate results.

01:34.870 --> 01:36.190
It is not that important.

01:36.190 --> 01:42.390
It is just an intermediate step that we have done in order to have our extra copy of the data, to manipulate

01:42.390 --> 01:46.710
it and so on, in order to prepare it to be inserted in the data warehouse.

01:46.710 --> 01:52.190
So after we loaded it in the data warehouse, this copy of the data is not any more important.

01:52.190 --> 01:54.110
It shouldn't stay like for a long time.

01:54.310 --> 02:00.110
That's why in this scenario, maybe we can go and use the temporary tables instead of normal tables

02:00.110 --> 02:01.510
for the intermediate results.

02:01.510 --> 02:07.350
And that's because only of one advantage that the database is going to go and do an automatic clean

02:07.390 --> 02:09.750
up after the whole session ends.

02:09.750 --> 02:12.790
So it comes out of the box automatically from the database.

02:12.790 --> 02:18.110
So that means I don't have to deal with that dropping mechanism of this table for the next load.

02:18.110 --> 02:22.990
If there is like something wrong in the data warehouse, you would like always to check the copy where

02:22.990 --> 02:26.510
the transformations are done in order to debug and find issues.

02:26.510 --> 02:31.670
So I don't normally use temporary tables in this scenarios, I use just normal tables, but for other

02:31.670 --> 02:33.590
small projects maybe this makes sense.

02:33.590 --> 02:38.070
So this is one use case on when to use the temporary tables in your projects.

02:38.070 --> 02:43.630
We use it in order to store intermediate results temporary until we are done with the session.

02:43.630 --> 02:47.870
And then once we are done, the database can go and drop that temporary table.
